{:id :EACL-FORMAL-017
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :manual-review
 :seed-or-trace
 "verified-authoritative/subproblem-lookup/unrepresented-registered-flight"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 worktree after EACL-FORMAL-016 and before coordinator-aware lookup"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "The lifecycle-stable generated lookup input was derived only from the tier's represented entry. A valid same-key flight can remain registered after tier admission rejects it. A second resolver therefore received generated start-computation even though host flight arbitration later forced it to join, so the generated decision was still not authoritative and read/write contention could take an unnecessary failed installation path."
 :fix
 "Resolution selection now reads the represented entry and lifecycle-qualified coordinator flight under the same store linearization lock. A complete represented entry selects use-completed-value; either an incomplete represented entry or a registered unrepresented flight selects join-computation; only the absence of both selects start-computation. A defensive flight-install collision re-dispatches the generated computing-state decision instead of hard-coding join."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.subproblem-cache-test/cache-unadmitted-fallbacks-still-share-one-flight-test"
  "formal mutation :unrepresented-flight-ignored-by-lookup"
  "formal/dafny/SubproblemCache.dfy RegisteredUnrepresentedFlightIsJoined"]}
